'' T39, RUN: a UDT whose 'operator cast' returns a USTRING reaches PRINT and '&' as a
'' ustring. The item's type is the UDT, so every consumer took it as narrow and printed
'' the UTF-16 bytes with the character count as a byte count: '(', NUL, '4', NUL, ','.
'' Now PRINT picks fb_PrintUstring for it, and a concatenation with one in it is a
'' ustring chain whose term is that cast's descriptor -- into a string or a ustring, with
'' a rendered number, and beside a type that also casts to long. Output identical to
'' fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/print-udt-ustr-cast.bas -o tests/codegen/printudtustrcast.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/printudtustrcast.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/printudtustrcast.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: a=(4, 6)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6)!
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6) w3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6) 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: b=w3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: x(4, 6)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6) 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6)(4, 6)
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: n=(4, 6)5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: (4, 6)w3
